# Absolute Virtue's protection (CR 702.16e, 702.16k) and Ancient Adamantoise's redirection ("All damage that would be dealt to
# you ... is dealt to this creature instead") both apply to the 1 combat damage Bot2's Fanatical Firebrand would deal to
# Bot1, and Bot1, the affected player, chooses which applies first (CR 616.1). Bot1 has the redirection apply first: the
# damage would now be dealt to the Adamantoise, which has no protection (the protection is its controller's, not its
# permanents'), so the Adamantoise is dealt 1 and nothing is prevented (CR 616.1f). The other order is
# absolute-virtue-and-ancient-adamantoise-its-controller-prevents-the-damage-first.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Island
Show and Tell
Ancient Adamantoise
Mox Ruby
Absolute Virtue
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Fanatical Firebrand
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Ancient Adamantoise)
Bot2.Choose()
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Absolute Virtue.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Fanatical Firebrand.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Attack(Fanatical Firebrand > Bot1)
Bot1.Replace(Ancient Adamantoise)
[T6 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Ancient Adamantoise.Damage = 1
Prevented = (absent)
